<BaseLayout title="Under The Surface" description="How Hyphos connects records, evidence and continuity: knowledge in context, traceable sources and a working record that carries between sessions.">
<section class="product-editorial-hero page-shell"><p class="section-label">Under The Surface</p><h1>Connect The Record<br />To The Reason</h1><p>The architecture follows the work: where information comes from, what it means in context and what needs to happen next.</p></section>
<section class="product-editorial-body page-shell"><aside class="product-editorial-aside"><p class="section-label">The Organizing Idea</p><p>An engagement brings the work together: the people, documents, meetings, decisions and deliverables that belong to it.</p></aside><div class="product-editorial-prose"><h2>Knowledge In Context</h2><p>Hyphos uses a knowledge graph to connect the records behind an engagement. A decision can be linked to its source meeting, the document it changes and the person responsible for the next step.</p><p>Those relationships help make a retrieved fact useful in the situation where someone needs it.</p><h2>Sources Close To The Answer</h2><p>Search and summaries help locate relevant information. The underlying source is the record to check.</p><p>The aim is to let a person follow the answer back to the evidence and understand what is supported, what has changed and what is still uncertain.</p><h2>Access Through The Working Tools</h2><p>Hyphos exposes capabilities through MCP, so compatible AI clients can work with its knowledge and tools. The integrations and access needed for a particular workflow are part of the pilot scope.</p><p>The goal is to keep the relevant context close to where the work is happening.</p></div></section>
<section id="domas" class="architecture-band"><div class="page-shell"><div><span class="section-label">Domas / Build & Evolve</span><h2>Build Hyphos Around<br />Your Business</h2></div><p>Domas is the build and adaptation capability behind Hyphos. It brings your workflows, terminology, integrations and requirements into how the platform is planned, built and reviewed. It also carries the evidence, decisions and work state forward, so the next change starts with what has already been learned.</p></div></section>
<section class="product-editorial-body page-shell"><aside class="product-editorial-aside"><p class="section-label">Learning Through The Work</p></aside><div class="product-editorial-prose"><h2>Keep Adapting As The Business Changes</h2><p>A correction often contains experience that a template misses. Hyphos is being developed to connect those lessons to future work, making the reasoning behind a good result easier to reuse and teach.</p><h2>Define The Boundaries Together</h2><p>A pilot should establish the sources it can use, the people who can access them and the actions that need human review. The specific deployment and integration requirements belong in that discussion.</p><a href="/contact" class="button button--gold">Discuss Your Workflow ↗</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
